+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PQz9tadyyd58JwyRcoXAoq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T1: CLI Time Tracker\n2\t\n3\t**Category:** greenfield/simple\n4\t**Timeout:** 10 minutes\n5\t**Tests:** 25\n6\t\n7\t## Objective\n8\t\n9\tBuild a command-line time tracking tool as a TypeScript library. All source code goes in `src/`.\n10\t\n11\t## Requirements\n12\t\n13\tImplement a `TimeTracker` class in `src/index.ts` that is exported (along with an `Entry` interface) with the following API:\n14\t\n15\t### Entry Interface\n16\t\n17\t```typescript\n18\tinterface Entry {\n19\t  taskName: string;   // Name of the tracked task\n20\t  startTime: string;  // ISO 8601 timestamp\n21\t  endTime: string | null; // ISO 8601 timestamp, or null if still running\n22\t}\n23\t```\n24\t\n25\t### TimeTracker Class\n26\t\n27\t```typescript\n28\tclass TimeTracker {\n29\t  constructor(filePath: string)\n30\t  start(taskName: string): Entry\n31\t  stop(): Entry\n32\t  getActiveTask(): Entry | null\n33\t  getLog(options?: { since?: Date }): Entry[]\n34\t  getSummary(): Record<string, number>\n35\t}\n36\t```\n37\t\n38\t### Behavior\n39\t\n40\t1. **constructor(filePath)** - Creates a tracker that persists data to the given JSON file path. The file and any parent directories should be created automatically when data is first written.\n41\t\n42\t2. **start(taskName)** - Starts tracking a new task. Returns the created entry.\n43\t   - If a task is already running, it must be auto-stopped before the new one starts.\n44\t   - Throws an error if `taskName` is empty.\n45\t   - Unicode task names must be supported.\n46\t\n47\t3. **stop()** - Stops the currently running task. Returns the stopped entry.\n48\t   - Throws an error if no task is currently running.\n49\t\n50\t4. **getActiveTask()** - Returns the currently running entry, or `null` if nothing is active.\n51\t\n52\t5. **getLog(options?)** - Returns all tracked entries.\n53\t   - If `options.since` is provided, filters to entries that:\n54\t     - Started on or after the `since` date, OR\n55\t     - Are still running (endTime is null), OR\n56\t     - Have an endTime on or after the `since` date (spanning the boundary)\n57\t\n58\t6. **getSummary()** - Returns an object keyed by task name with total duration in milliseconds.\n59\t   - Multiple entries with the same task name have their durations summed.\n60\t   - For running tasks (no endTime), use the current time to calculate duration.\n61\t   - Returns an empty object if there are no entries.\n62\t\n63\t### Persistence\n64\t\n65\t- Data is stored as JSON in the file specified by the constructor.\n66\t- Creating a new `TimeTracker` instance with the same file path must load existing data.\n67\t- The file and parent directories are created on first write if they don't exist.\n68\t\n69\t## Validation\n70\t\n71\tRun `npm test` to execute the test suite. All 25 tests must pass.\n72\t\n73\tRun `npm run build` to verify TypeScript compilation.\n74\t\n75\tRun `npm run lint` to verify code quality.\n76\t\n77\t## Constraints\n78\t\n79\t- All code must be in `src/` directory\n80\t- Must compile with the provided `tsconfig.json` (strict mode, ES2022, Node16 modules)\n81\t- Must pass the provided ESLint configuration\n82\t- No additional dependencies may be added (use only Node.js built-in modules)\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_017LFE8sBh3JqwfWtxb9Umay","session_id":"f5c8e4a4-7cd4-436d-913a-1a4f82849400","uuid":"d123efb5-78ef-4825-ad76-885bedf875a6","timestamp":"2026-07-25T01:15:30.066Z","subagent_type":"conclave:code-reviewer","task_description":"Review time tracker implementation"}
